 SFTP is mainly used to collect or transfer performance data files, whilst the REST API is used for remote operation, maintenance and Request/Response (R/R) Communication. During R/R communication, the request is transmitted from the OSS through the EMS to the NEs, and the response is transmitted from the NEs, through the EMS and to the OSS.Management Interface Architecture1.2 Interface ProtocolThe following describes the communication pattern between OSS and EMS and the protocol for each communication pattern in the Northbound Interface.Interface Protocol Communication Pattern NotificationSNMP Trap (SNMP over UDP) is used as a notification method from EMS to OSS.The SNMP trap is configured as follows.SNMP Protocol DefinitionItemsDefinitionDescriptionSNMP VersionSNMPv3RFC 3410AgentEMSManagerOSSTrap target port162 / UDPOther port number are also availableAuthentication method(*)USM��MD5��Engine ID(*)0x8000137001 + <EMS IP Address>: 18 hexadecimal values.< EMS IP Address >: The IP address of the sender used when notifying the EMS to OSS- MCMA/MCMS��?NBI_VIPFor example, , If the IP address is 127.0.0.1,0x80001370017f000001=0x800137001 + 7f (127 (Dec)) + 00 (0 (Dec)) + 00 (0 (Dec)) + 01 (1 (Dec)).(*) SNMPv2c is unnecessary.Security method is only authenticated by user / password, and the SNMP message encryption is not performed (however, password encryption is performed). For password encryption methods, use MD5. The sequence of SNMP trap for notification is as follows.Notification Sequence RESTfulThe OSS uses RESTful as a Request / Response method for EMS.The OSS performs the request through the URL of the EMS and the EMS responds for the request.The EMS use HTTPs basic Authentication for the REST API In Authentication, EMS use HTTPs protocol, which encrypts the HTTP with the password.  HTTP Basic authentication uses standard fields in the HTTP header.The RESTful protocol regulations ar